    <innerclass refid="classhorus__generator__pattern_1_1Waypoints" prot="public">horus_generator_pattern::Waypoints</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacehorus__generator__pattern">horus_generator_pattern</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Generator plugin that follows joint waypoints (home, sit, stand, recorded gaits). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Waypoints come from YAML (<computeroutput>times</computeroutput> + flat <computeroutput>positions</computeroutput>, one row of <computeroutput>joints</computeroutput> per time) or from a CSV file (<computeroutput>time, j1, j2, ...</computeroutput>, optional header naming the joints). <computeroutput>quantity</computeroutput> says what they are: <computeroutput>position</computeroutput> (default) and <computeroutput>effort</computeroutput> waypoints are interpolated and output as they are; with <computeroutput>velocity</computeroutput> the waypoints are positions and the output is their time derivative (scaled by the live speed), for velocity-controlled joints. Between waypoints the output is interpolated linearly or smoothly (cosine ease: zero velocity at every waypoint). With <computeroutput>start_from_current</computeroutput>, the first waypoint is replaced by the measured joint positions when the behavior starts, so a &quot;home&quot; behavior works from wherever the robot is. A non-cycling trajectory finishes at its last waypoint; a cycling one restarts from the first. Playback speed is the generator_server&apos;s live <computeroutput>speed_scale</computeroutput> (it scales the time this plugin is given). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
